WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.259 --> 00:00:16.340
The Game of Thrones prequels are coming and
it brings us many legendary characters.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.900
We have House of the Dragon and Tales of Dunk
and Egg coming our way.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:25.519
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:29.610
to air in 2022.
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:34.809
as showrunners and executive producers. George
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive

00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:38.940
producer.
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:43.520
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:47.920
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.569
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold

00:00:52.569 --> 00:00:57.679
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”

00:00:57.679 --> 00:01:02.089
Thats Fire And Blood volume 1.
The yet unreleased Fire And Vlood volume 2

00:01:02.089 --> 00:01:07.380
will continue from where part 1 ended, with
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:13.080
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:19.030
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.
HBO is also developing a new Game of Thrones

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:23.620
prequel show based on George R.R. Martin’s
Tales of Dunk and Egg, which follow the adventures

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:28.970
of Ser Duncan the Tall (Dunk)
and young Aegon V Targaryen (Egg) 90 years

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:31.990
prior to the events of “A Song of Ice and
Fire.”

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:37.040
In this video we talk about a character that
is important in both, the Targaryen history

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.900
and the tales of Dunk and Egg (being the main
character himself), Aegon Egg Targaryen. Aegon

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:47.640
V Targaryen was a Lord of the Seven Kingdoms
and the fifteenth Targaryen to sit the Iron

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:53.010
Throne as King of the Andals, the Rhoynar,
and the First Men. In his youth, he went by

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:58.980
the nickname Egg and squired for Ser Duncan
the Tall. Aegon became king after a Great

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:04.600
Council bypassed a number of candidates earlier
in the line of succession, and after his elder

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:11.020
brother, Maester Aemon, refused the throne.
As the fourth son of Maekar I, himself a fourth

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:16.880
son, Aegon was called Aegon the Unlikely.
Aegon had large eyes which could appear dark

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.889
blue, but were actually deep and dark and
purple. The boy was pasty faced and skinny.

00:02:22.889 --> 00:02:28.040
He shaved his hair to hide his identity while
a squire, making his eyes appear huge on his

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:34.000
bald head. Aegon wore a wide-brimmed floppy
straw hat while squiring for Ser Duncan the

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.920
Tall. According to a semi-canonical source,
the adult Aegon had long, shoulder-length

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:45.900
hair that shone like beaten gold with strands
of silver woven together. Tall, slender and

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:51.489
handsome, he wore the crown of Aegon III.
Aegon grew to become a kindly and approachable

00:02:51.489 --> 00:02:57.599
man beloved by smallfolk. Maester Aemon, who
gave the nickname Egg to his brother, believed

00:02:57.599 --> 00:03:12.480
that Aegon had innocence and sweetness.
Aegon was born the fourth son and fifth child

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:18.829
of Prince Maekar Targaryen and his wife, Dyanna
Dayne. Aegon served at court in King's Landing

00:03:18.829 --> 00:03:25.010
for two years as a page, sometimes attending
to the small council. Aegon owned a dragon

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:29.620
egg, which was colored with green and white
swirls and had been placed in his cradle with

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:35.680
him when he was a babe. Aegon and his elder
brother, Prince Aemon who we all know as Maester

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:41.209
Aemon, hoped their eggs would hatch so they
could become dragonriders. Aegon kept his

00:03:41.209 --> 00:03:47.529
egg at Summerhall. Aegon loathed his brother,
the cruel and sadistic Aerion. Aegon was supposed

00:03:47.529 --> 00:03:52.879
to squire for his eldest brother, Daeron,
in the tourney at Ashford Meadow, but Daeron

00:03:52.879 --> 00:03:59.309
had no interest in jousting and instead drank
himself into a stupor at an inn. Daeron shaved

00:03:59.309 --> 00:04:05.019
Aegon's head to prevent the boy's distinctive
Targaryen hair from being recognized by men

00:04:05.019 --> 00:04:11.049
sent by their father, Prince Maekar. When
the hedge knight Dunk visited the inn, he

00:04:11.049 --> 00:04:16.450
assumed Aegon was a stableboy. Calling himself
"Egg", the disguised Aegon had assumed that

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:22.510
Dunk was short for "Duncan", which Dunk accepted.
Aegon was impressed by the humble hedge knight

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:28.090
and followed him. Ser Duncan the Tall agreed
to let Egg serve as his squire during the

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:33.830
tourney. Duncan was arrested and sentenced
to fight a trial by battle after attacking

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:39.670
Egg's elder brother, Prince Aerion Targaryen.
Duncan was accused by both Aerion and his

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:45.050
older brother, Prince Daeron Targaryen, who
had falsely accused Duncan of having kidnapped

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:50.560
Prince Aegon Targaryen. Because the battle
was to be a Trial of Seven, Aegon convinced

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:57.350
Ser Lyonel Baratheon to fight on behalf of
Duncan. Aegon's uncle, Prince Baelor Breakspear,

00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:03.170
also fought alongside Duncan during the trial,
but Baelor died of a wound inflicted by Prince

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:08.430
Maekar, Baelor's brother and Aegon's father,
who had fought on behalf of Aerion and House

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:14.360
Targaryen. After Daeron was defeated and Aerion
withdrew his accusation during the trial,

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:19.660
Duncan was declared innocent. Maekar, the
Prince of Summerhall, wished Aegon to be trained

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:24.500
as a knight, but Aegon would only agree if
Duncan were the knight who trained him. When

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:29.930
Maekar offered Duncan a place at the garrison
of Summerhall, Dunk declined and agreed to

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:36.040
take Aegon on only if Aegon accompanied him
as his squire. Aegon would live humbly, but

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:40.930
Duncan thought it would make Aegon a better
man than his brothers, Aerion and Daeron.

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:46.930
Thus, Aegon served as a squire to the Duncan
under his nickname "Egg". Aegon kept his identity

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:51.940
secret from the public while squiring for
Duncan, and he kept hidden in his boot a signet

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:58.280
ring from his father, Maekar Targaryen, Prince
of Summerhall. Aegon married Lady Betha Blackwood

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:03.930
in 220 AC. The marriage at the time provoked
no opposition as Aegon was very low in the

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:09.560
line of succession. They married for love
and eventually had five children together.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:16.350
Aegon named his first-born son Duncan to honor
his friend, Ser Duncan the Tall. In 221 AC,

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:21.590
Aegon's uncle, King Aerys I Targaryen died
with no issue and was followed on the Iron

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:27.770
Throne by his last living brother, Prince
Maekar Targayen. Aegon and his brothers were

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:34.270
summoned to court by King Maekar. According
to a semi-canon source, Aegon participated

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:40.970
in the suppression of the Peake Uprising in
233 AC, with Tion Lannister as his squire.

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:47.190
King Maekar I was killed at Starpike during
the rebellion, however. According to a semi-canon

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:52.870
source, the prince knighted the mortally wounded
Tywald Lannister, Tion's twin, during the

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:58.310
battle. With Maekar dead, it was unclear who
should be the king since two of Aegon's older

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:04.720
brothers had died before his father. Daeron
left a feeble-witted daughter named Vaella

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:10.900
and Aerion an infant son, so a Great Council
was called to choose a king. Aegon seemed

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:16.380
the logical choice, but many lords considered
him "half a peasant" due to his youth among

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:22.830
the smallfolk. The council approached Aegon's
older brother, Maester Aemon, but he refused,

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:27.550
stating the crown should be given to Aegon.
Aegon was crowned Lord of the Seven Kingdoms

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:35.150
in 233 AC when he was thirty-three years old.
During most, if not all, of Aegon V's reign,

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:39.830
his old friend Ser Duncan the Tall served
as Lord Commander of the Kingsguard. Aegon's

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:45.690
first act as king was the arrest of Lord Brynden
Rivers, the Hand of the King, for the murder

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:51.660
of Aenys Blackfyre, as Bloodraven had offered
Aenys safe conduct to Westeros for the Great

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:57.090
Council, but had Aenys executed when he arrived
in the capital. Although all were glad another

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:02.900
Blackfyre pretender was dead, Aegon had to
punish Lord Bloodraven to prove the word of

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:08.940
the Iron Throne was not worthless. Although
Brynden was sentenced to death, Aegon allowed

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:14.560
him to join the Night's Watch. Aegon's brother,
Maester Aemon, decided to join the Watch as

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:20.280
well, to prevent any plots in which he would
be used against his brother. Brynden and Aemon

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:25.580
were joined by many of Bloodraven's personal
guard, the Raven's Teeth, as well as prisoners

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:30.650
released from dungeons by the king. The end
of winter saw the return of the Blackfyre

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:38.139
Pretenders, with the Fourth Blackfyre Rebellion
taking place in 236 AC. Daemon III Blackfyre

00:08:38.139 --> 00:08:43.979
attempted to seize the Iron Throne with the
Golden Company, but few rallied to his side.

00:08:43.979 --> 00:08:49.230
Aegon and his sons rode to meet and repel
the invaders, and Duncan the Tall slew Daemon

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:55.140
in single combat, ending the rebellion. Aegor
Rivers, known as Bittersteel, managed to flee

00:08:55.140 --> 00:09:00.500
with remnants of the Golden Company across
the narrow sea. Aegon V spent much of his

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:06.400
reign dealing with uprisings. Most of Aegon's
troubles resulted from his efforts to improve

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:12.510
the lives of the smallfolk, whom he had interacted
with while squiring for Duncan. Lacking the

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:18.860
dragons controlled by early Targaryen kings,
Aegon reluctantly compromised with the disobedient

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:25.880
lords on several issues. Aegon faced renewed
troubles in his reign caused by his sons.

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:31.050
Convinced the Targaryen practice of incestuous
marriage was harmful after spending time with

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:35.800
smallfolk, Aegon and his queen, Betha Blackwood,
betrothed four of their children to some of

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:41.580
the Great Houses of the Seven Kingdoms in
237 AC. Their eldest son and heir, Prince

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:47.360
Duncan, was betrothed to the daughter of Lord
Lyonel Baratheon of Storm's End. Prince Jaehaerys,

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:53.950
Aegon's second son, was betrothed to Lady
Celia Tully, the daughter of the Lord of Riverrun.

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:59.300
Aegon's youngest son, Prince Daeron, was betrothed
to Lady Olenna Redwyne of the Arbor who would

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:07.210
later become known to us all as Lady Olenna
Tyrell.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:34.551
In addition, Aegon's eldest daughter, Princess
Shaera, was betrothed to Luthor Tyrell, the

00:10:34.551 --> 00:10:39.740
heir to Highgarden. The proposed marriages
would have won Aegon much support for his

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:46.150
reforms, but his children had inherited his
willfulness and their mother's stubbornness.

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:52.040
Beginning in 239 AC, Prince Duncan fell in
love with and eventually wed the mysterious

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:57.650
Jenny of Oldstones. The prince chose his wife
over the Iron Throne and abdicated as Prince

00:10:57.650 --> 00:11:03.000
of Dragonstone, making his younger brother,
Prince Jaehaerys, the new heir. With Duncan

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:08.540
refusing to marry the daughter of Lord Baratheon,
Storm's End briefly rose in rebellion, which

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:14.450
ended when Ser Duncan the Tall of the Kingsguard
forced Lord Lyonel to yield during trial by

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:20.870
combat. With Duncan marrying Jenny as precedent,
Jaehaerys and Shaera secretly wed and consummated

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:27.430
their marriage in 240 AC, leaving Aegon to
deal with the anger of Houses Tully and Tyrell.

00:11:27.430 --> 00:11:33.000
Although betrothed for nine years to Lady
Olenna Redwyne, Prince Daeron broke his betrothal

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:41.430
in 246 AC. In 258 AC, nine outlaws, exiles,
pirates and sellswords hoping to carve out

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:47.570
individual kingdoms came together in the Disputed
Lands of Essos. Among these Band of Nine was

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:54.700
Maelys I Blackfyre, the last of the Blackfyres.
Because the outlaws had no great urgency,

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:59.950
King Aegon remained intent on his reign and
on dragons in particular. Against the advice

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:05.760
of his friends and counselors, Aegon V became
convinced that only with dragons could he

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:11.300
force the lords of the Seven Kingdoms to accept
his decrees that granted freedoms, rights,

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:17.990
and protections to the smallfolk. This eventually
led to the tragedy of Summerhall in 259 AC,

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:23.860
in which Aegon perished while trying to hatch
dragon eggs. His son, Prince Duncan the Small;

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:27.550
his friend and Lord Commander of the Kingsguard,
Ser Duncan the Tall;

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:32.940
and others of the royal court also perished
in the fire. Aegon was succeeded by his second

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:39.310
son and heir, Jaehaerys II. Many of the laws,
rights and protections King Aegon V had granted

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:44.760
and bestowed upon the smallfolk were later
undone during the reign of King Aerys II by

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:50.840
the Hand of the King, Lord Tywin Lannister.
Many interesting characters, Targaryens and

00:12:50.840 --> 00:12:56.480
others, many legendary figures that are immortalized
in many songs and stories - all of that and

00:12:56.480 --> 00:13:00.850
more the Game of Thrones prequel shows are
bringing to us, starting with the House of

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:05.330
the Dragon in 2022. Thank you so much for
watching, hope you enjoyed this video and

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:08.820
if you did make sure to give it a big thumbs
upand I hope to see you in the next one, peace!

